==============================================================================
S3  multi-affine two-rooted identity:  [prod_{p in S} w_p](d^2_{J0 Jt} log Z) = mu(G_S)
==============================================================================
  150 instances: violations = 0
  => the two-rooted coefficient is the SINGLE-rooted Ursell coefficient mu(G_S), i.e. GO1's
     (-1)^(|S|-1) N(G_S); it is zero unless both roots lie in S.  No new identity, but the
     exact placement of N inside the two-point expansion is pinned.

  EVALUATION GAP (exact toy, 2 adjacent plaquettes, no other):
     Z = 1 + w_0 + w_1 ;  C = -w_1 w_0 / Z^2  (analytic, at J=0)
     multi-affine sum at w_p = w:   mu(edge) w^2 = -w^2  (one term only)
     machine check 1/(1+2w)^2 = w^0:1, w^1:-4, w^2:12, w^3:-32, w^4:80
     => analytic C(w) = -w^2/(1+2w)^2 has w^3..w^4 coeffs 4,-12  != 0 = multi-affine sum's higher coefficients.
     => the multi-affine sum is NOT the evaluation at a common activity; the difference is
        the repeated-plaquette terms (w_p^2 = 0 truncation).  N enters at coefficient level only.

