==============================================================================
S6  2D witness for the no-go on all-positive counting representations
==============================================================================
  S = {p0}:  N = 1 and weight w > 0  =>  every  sum_S a_S w^|S| N(G_S)  with a_S >= 0 is >= w > 0,
  in every dimension.  2D pure SU(N) YM has  f1^2(tr F^2) == 0  identically (ATOM2:15,62-63 [T]).
  => f1^2 admits no all-positive NBC representation.  Only the alternating form survives,
     and there positivity is exactly the domination problem (not a count).

