==============================================================================
  neighbourhood: 3750 plaquettes;  deg(p0) = 20  (must be 20 for d=4)
  roots separated by 1:  k=2: #S=     1, sum N=1;  k=3: #S=    34, sum N=38;  k=4: #S=   982, sum N=1304;  k=5: #S= 26975, sum N=44111
  roots separated by 2:  k=2: #S=     1, sum N=0;  k=3: #S=    34, sum N=1;  k=4: #S=   968, sum N=51;  k=5: #S= 26257, sum N=2074
  separation 3: target not in window

  BYPRODUCT:  |phi^U(tube_T)| = N_T  with n = 4T, so  |c_Gamma|^{1/n} = N_T^{1/(4T)}
     closed form from the recurrence:  N_T = A*lambda+^T + B*lambda-^T,  lambda+- = 23 +- 2*sqrt(111) = 44.0713075057, 1.9286924943
     =>  lim_T N_T^(1/(4T)) = lambda+^(1/4) = 2.57655243
     corpus lower bound (GV2 4.2(A), K_6): 120^(1/6) = 2.22090615
     =>  lambda_Ur >= 2.57655243  >  2.220906  (STRICT improvement)
     SU(2) convention u=0.625:  lambda_Ur*u >= 1.610345 > 1   (corpus had 1.388066)

